✅ Fix: Change Docker root directory
1. Stop Docker service
sudo systemctl stop docker
 
2. Create new directory (if not exists)
sudo mkdir -p /app/docker
Set correct permissions:
sudo chown root:root /app/docker

3. Move existing Docker data (IMPORTANT if you have containers/images)
sudo rsync -aP /var/lib/docker/ /app/docker/

or 

sudo cp -a /var/lib/docker/. /app/docker/

4. Configure Docker daemon
Edit or create this file:
sudo nano /etc/docker/daemon.json
Add:
{
  "data-root": "/app/docker"
}
 
5. Start Docker again
sudo systemctl start docker
 
6. Verify
docker info | grep "Docker Root Dir"
You should see:
Docker Root Dir: /app/docker
 
Check location used space
sudo du -sh /var/lib/docker
sudo du -sh /app/docker
sudo du -sh /var/lib/containerd

Optional cleanup (after confirming everything works)
sudo rm -rf /var/lib/docker


✅  Pre download ollama model restore into the server

1. Find model storage on dev PC
docker volume  ls
DRIVER    VOLUME NAME
local     self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_n8n_storage
local     self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_ollama_storage
local     self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_postgres_storage
local     self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_qdrant_storage

📁 3. Stop Ollama (important)
systemctl stop ollama

or Docker:

docker stop ollama

4. Copy models to server

You can also archive models:

Cd /app/

sudo tar -czvf ollama-models.tar.gz \
/var/lib/docker/volumes/self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_ollama_storage/_data


Then transfer:

scp ollama-models.tar.gz user@server:/app/

from windows: 
scp C:\Users\mr111802\Documents\ollama\ollama-models.tar.gz appadmin@192.168.202.168:/app/ollama/ollama-models.tar.gz

5. On server start Ollama
ollama list
docker exec -it ollama ollama list

If everything is correct, model will appear immediately.

Extract the model into Server
cd /app/docker/volumes/self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_ollama_storage/_data

rm -rf *

sudo tar -xzvf ollama-models_20260428.tar.gz \
-C /app/docker/volumes/self-hosted-ai-starter-kit_ollama_storage/_data

Verify
docker exec -it ollama ollama list




